     "Christianity became one of the religious traditions represented among some Sogdian communities. Surviving manuscripts, inscriptions, and archaeological discoveries provide evidence of Christian life in the region.",
     "The church also reached areas around the Tarim Basin, including settlements along the southern and northern routes of the Silk Road.",
     "Christian manuscripts and inscriptions discovered in Central Asia reveal that believers adapted their religious practices to local circumstances. Their communities used local languages, artistic styles, and forms of expression while remaining connected to the wider eastern Christian tradition.",
