     "Christianity became established among some Sogdian communities through connections with the Church of the East.",
     "One important center was Samarkand.",
     "Samarkand was one of the great cities of Central Asia. Its strategic location made it a major meeting point for merchants and travelers. The city was connected to the commercial networks that extended westward toward Persia and eastward toward China.",
