     "Genghis Khan began building an empire that would transform the history of Asia.",
     "His armies expanded into northern China, Central Asia, Persia, and territories farther west. Within a few generations, the Mongol Empire became one of the largest connected land empires in history.",
     "The expansion brought many different peoples under Mongol authority.",
     "The empire included Chinese farmers and administrators, Persian scholars, Central Asian merchants, Turkic communities, Muslim populations, Buddhists, Christians, and people who followed traditional religious practices.",
     "The Mongol rulers had to govern this enormous diversity.",
