     "John of Montecorvino was sent east as a missionary and representative of the Roman Catholic Church.",
     "He traveled through the Middle East and Central Asia before reaching China in 1294, during the reign of Kublai Khan.",
     "He arrived in the Yuan capital, known as Khanbaliq, which is associated with present-day Beijing.",
     "John’s arrival marked a major development in the history of Catholic Christianity in China.",
     "The earlier Tang Dynasty Christian movement had been associated with the Church of the East. John’s mission, however, belonged to the Latin Catholic tradition and was connected to the papacy in Rome.",
     "This distinction is important because Christianity in medieval China was not represented by only one tradition.",
     "John began establishing a Catholic community in the capital.",
     "He built a church, gathered believers, and devoted himself to preaching and teaching. He also worked to communicate Christian teaching to people who spoke languages different from his own.",
