     "Catholic Christianity in China experienced periods of hardship, particularly when imperial authorities became suspicious of foreign religious activity.",
     "The restrictions introduced during the Qing dynasty were influenced by several factors. The Chinese government was concerned about foreign influence, social stability, and the authority of the emperor. Religious disputes involving missionaries also contributed to tensions.",
