     "After Robert Morrison’s pioneering work, Protestant missionary activity gradually expanded during the nineteenth century.",
     "Missionaries arrived from Britain, the United States, and other countries. They represented different Protestant traditions, including Congregationalists, Baptists, Methodists, Presbyterians, and other Christian groups.",
     "Many missionaries believed that sharing the gospel involved more than preaching. They also established schools, hospitals, printing operations, and charitable institutions.",
