     "Medical missions were another important development. Missionary doctors established hospitals and clinics, treating illnesses and injuries and introducing medical practices that were becoming influential in the modern world.",
     "One important medical missionary was Peter Parker, an American physician who arrived in China in 1834. He established an ophthalmic hospital in Guangzhou in 1835. His medical work helped many patients and demonstrated how medical care could become a practical expression of Christian compassion.",
