     "Protestant churches established congregations throughout the country. Catholic communities also expanded, and the number of Korean priests, religious sisters, and lay leaders increased.",
     "South Korean churches became known for large prayer gatherings, early morning prayer meetings, Bible study, evangelism, and organized missionary activity.",
     "One of the most influential Protestant churches was Yoido Full Gospel Church in Seoul, associated with Pastor David Yonggi Cho. The church became internationally known for its large congregation and cell-group approach to ministry.",
