     "Catholic Christianity also experienced significant growth. Korean Catholic communities became increasingly active in education, social service, and public discussions about human dignity and justice.",
     "During the decades of authoritarian government in South Korea, some Christian leaders and communities participated in movements for democracy and human rights. Their involvement varied, but certain churches became important places for social criticism and public advocacy.",
