     "Despite these challenges, Xavier believed that Japan offered an important opportunity for the Christian mission in Asia. After approximately two years in Japan, he departed in 1551, intending to continue his work elsewhere in Asia. He died in 1552 on Shangchuan Island near the Chinese coast, before he could enter mainland China.",
