     "Protestant Christianity has also grown and diversified. Evangelical, Baptist, Methodist, Presbyterian, Pentecostal, and independent churches serve communities across the islands.",
     "The National Council of Churches in the Philippines has provided a platform for cooperation among several Protestant and non-Roman Catholic Christian traditions.",
     "The Philippines is also home to indigenous Christian movements and churches. One important example is the Iglesia ni Cristo, founded in 1914 by Felix Manalo.",
     "Iglesia ni Cristo has developed a substantial national and international presence. It has a distinct theology and ecclesiastical identity and should not be confused with mainstream Catholic or Protestant denominations.",
