     "Nevertheless, Christian communities continued to worship and maintain their religious identity. Local believers, pastors, priests, and families preserved Christian traditions through difficult circumstances.",
     "This period demonstrates how Christianity in Vietnam was affected by colonialism, revolution, national division, and war. It also reminds us that Christians were not a single political group and that their experiences cannot be reduced to one national or ideological position."
