     "Christianity continues to have an important presence in modern Vietnam, despite the political, cultural, and social changes that have shaped the country.",
     "The two largest Christian traditions are Roman Catholicism and Protestant Christianity.",
     "The Catholic Church has an established presence throughout Vietnam, with dioceses, parishes, religious orders, seminaries, schools, and charitable institutions. Vietnamese Catholics participate actively in worship, family religious life, education, and community service.",
     "The Church has also developed relationships with international Catholic institutions, including the Vatican. Diplomatic and ecclesiastical relations between Vietnam and the Holy See have evolved gradually, reflecting ongoing discussions about religious life and institutional cooperation.",
