     "Mission requires commitment. Early missionaries traveled through difficult conditions to share their faith.",
     "Faith should not be confused with political power. Christian witness must remain distinct from the pursuit of empire or economic control.",
     "Local believers matter. The establishment of churches depends on people who receive and live out the Gospel within their own communities.",
     "Patience is essential. Religious understanding develops through teaching, relationships, and time.",
     "God’s work can continue through uncertainty. Political changes do not necessarily destroy the faith of local communities."
