     "Judson initially worked with the intention of translating Christian Scripture and communicating the Gospel to Burmese-speaking communities. He studied the language and gradually developed the skills necessary to translate the Bible.",
     "The task was demanding. Burmese had a distinctive written tradition and a complex religious vocabulary shaped by centuries of Buddhist scholarship. Judson had to consider how Christian ideas could be expressed clearly without confusing them with existing religious concepts.",
