     "Cambodia endured the destruction of the Khmer Rouge era and subsequent conflicts. After 1979, the country experienced years of instability before moving toward a new political settlement through the Paris Peace Agreements of 1991 and the United Nations Transitional Authority in Cambodia during 1992–1993.",
     "Christian communities in Cambodia gradually rebuilt their institutions. Catholic churches, Protestant congregations, and Christian aid organizations contributed to education, rehabilitation, social care, and support for vulnerable people.",
