   "• 1 Corinthians 12:4–7 — Different gifts given by the same Spirit.",
   "• Romans 12:4–8 — Different members serving together in one body.",
   "• Galatians 6:9–10 — Continuing to do good and serve others faithfully.",
   "Final Reflection — Modern Asian Christian Movements",
   "The history of modern Asian Christian movements demonstrates the extraordinary diversity and resilience of Christianity throughout Asia.",
   "During the nineteenth, twentieth, and twenty-first centuries, Asian churches experienced revival, political change, persecution, institutional growth, theological renewal, and international expansion.",
   "The Korean revival movements demonstrated the importance of prayer, repentance, and spiritual renewal. Chinese Christians showed remarkable perseverance during periods of political pressure and religious restriction. Indian and Southeast Asian churches developed strong indigenous traditions shaped by local pastors, evangelists, educators, and community leaders.",
   "Pentecostal and charismatic movements brought new forms of worship, prayer, evangelism, and lay participation. Educational, medical, and humanitarian organizations demonstrated how Christian faith could contribute to the well-being of society.",
   "Asian Christian mission also became increasingly international. Churches that had once received missionaries began sending their own workers to other nations. Korean, Indian, Filipino, Chinese, and other Asian Christian communities became important contributors to global Christianity.",
   "Yet modern Christian movements must also examine their weaknesses. Church growth without accountability can lead to spiritual abuse. Mission without cultural respect can create unnecessary conflict. Humanitarian service without ethical responsibility can damage trust. Political pressure can threaten religious freedom, while internal divisions can weaken Christian witness.",
   "The most important lesson is that the strength of the church is not measured simply by buildings, membership numbers, financial resources, or international influence. True strength is found in faithfulness to Jesus Christ, sound biblical teaching, spiritual maturity, love, justice, humility, and service.",
   "Modern Asian Christianity remains a living and developing story. Its future will be shaped by believers who are willing to pray, learn, serve, lead responsibly, and share the Gospel with compassion.",
   "Final Reflection Questions",
   "• What are the most important developments in modern Asian Christianity?",
