     "One of the most influential developments in modern Asian Christianity has been the growth of Pentecostal and charismatic movements.",
     "Pentecostal Christianity emphasizes the work of the Holy Spirit, spiritual gifts, prayer, evangelism, healing, and personal transformation.",
     "The modern Pentecostal movement is often associated with the early twentieth-century revival at Azusa Street in Los Angeles, which began in 1906. The movement soon spread internationally through missionaries, travelers, and local believers.",
