     "In India, Pentecostal communities expanded during the early twentieth century. The Pentecostal Mission, various indigenous Pentecostal churches, and other Christian movements contributed to this growth.",
     "One important Indian Pentecostal leader was K. E. Abraham, who became associated with the Indian Pentecostal Church of God, established in 1925.",
     "The movement developed churches, Bible training institutions, and evangelistic networks in Kerala and other parts of India.",
     "Pentecostal Christianity also expanded in northeastern India, where local pastors and evangelists established congregations among different ethnic communities.",
     "In South Korea, Pentecostal Christianity became especially visible through the growth of large churches and prayer movements.",
     "David Yonggi Cho’s Yoido Full Gospel Church became an internationally known example of large-scale Pentecostal church development.",
     "Its emphasis on prayer, evangelism, cell groups, and lay participation influenced churches in many countries.",
     "In the Philippines, Pentecostal and charismatic movements developed within both independent churches and established Christian denominations.",
     "Some Catholic communities also experienced charismatic renewal, particularly through prayer groups and movements emphasizing spiritual gifts and personal devotion.",
     "In Indonesia, Pentecostal and charismatic churches grew in several regions, particularly in urban areas and among younger Christian communities.",
