     "The Batak Christian Protestant Church, known as HKBP, became one of the largest Protestant churches in Indonesia.",
     "Its development was strongly associated with the work of Ludwig Ingwer Nommensen, but Batak Christian leaders and congregations shaped its long-term growth.",
     "In the Philippines, Catholic Christianity remained dominant, but Protestant and evangelical churches developed new indigenous forms of worship, evangelism, and community service.",
     "The Jesus Is Lord Church, founded by Eddie Villanueva in 1978, became one of the notable Filipino evangelical movements.",
     "The Philippines also developed extensive networks of Christian organizations serving migrant workers, poor communities, and people affected by disasters.",
     "In Vietnam, Protestant Christianity continued to develop among communities including the Hmong and other ethnic minorities, as well as urban congregations.",
