     "Christianity expanded significantly during the nineteenth and twentieth centuries. Protestant and Catholic communities became important in national education, public life, and social reform.",
     "Although Christians are a substantial minority of South Korea’s population rather than a majority, Christian institutions have had considerable influence.",
     "South Korean churches have also become important in international missionary activity, theological education, and global Christian worship.",
