     "For much of its modern history, Nepal was governed by a monarchy that maintained a close relationship between the state and Hindu religious identity. Hindu traditions influenced the royal institution, public ceremonies, and national culture. This shaped the legal and social environment in which Christians lived.",
     "The modern history of Christianity in Nepal developed under restrictions on religious conversion and missionary activity. Foreign missionaries were generally not permitted to establish an unrestricted presence, and Christian communities had to operate within a legal environment that protected the established religious order.",
     "Catholic Christians were among the early organized Christian communities in the wider Himalayan region. However, their work in Nepal remained limited for long periods. The country was not open to the same kind of foreign missionary expansion that occurred in British India.",
