     "To understand the wider Christian background of the lands that became Pakistan, it is important to understand the history of Christianity in Persia. Persia was a major civilization situated between the Mediterranean world and South Asia. Its cities, roads, trading networks, and political relationships connected regions that today belong to several different countries.",
     "Christianity reached Persian territories during the early centuries of the church. Over time, Christian communities developed in important centers such as Seleucia-Ctesiphon and other urban areas. These communities worshiped in languages used throughout the region, especially Syriac, and developed traditions of theology, biblical interpretation, liturgy, and education.",
