     "Education played a central role in the aspirations of many Christian families. Parents hoped that their children would receive opportunities that had been unavailable to earlier generations. Church schools and other educational institutions helped some families gain access to learning and professional life. Teachers, pastors, and community leaders often encouraged young people to pursue education and serve society.",
