     "The dignity of Dalit Christians must be recognized without defining them only through suffering. Their communities have produced families, leaders, pastors, teachers, musicians, and workers whose lives demonstrate faith, resilience, and service. Their history is not merely a story of oppression but also a story of agency, courage, and spiritual identity.",
